  "id": "COMPOUND:3295 - PROTEIN:4740",
  "verbalization": "Flavopiridol is implicated in the regulation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase pim-3 through a multi-step pathway involving Sinocalycanchinensin G. The evidence suggests that flavopiridol directly targets Serine/threonine-protein kinase RIO2, which in turn is targeted by Sinocalycanchinensin G. This kinase pim-3 is ultimately targeted by Sinocalycanchinensin G, establishing a chain of interactions that links flavopiridol to pim-3 via the intermediate of RIO2. The presence of multiple pathways with similar intermediate nodes (Sinocalycanchinensin G) supports a functional role for these compounds in modulating pim-3 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for flavopiridol to influence pim-3 through a complex network of kinase targets, emphasizing the importance of Sinocalycanchinensin G as a central mediator in this relationship.",
